course: dictionary
lesson: 12471
title: Changing shape
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To deform something means to change its normal shape, often by bending, squashing or stretching it. The word is a verb, so you can write deform, deforms, deformed or deforming. «The heat deformed the plastic ruler.» The ruler was straight before the heat, and after it the ruler is no longer the right shape.
explain: Some things go back to their shape and some do not. A rubber band is elastic, so it springs back after you stretch it. Modelling clay is plastic, so when you squash it, it stays squashed. We say the clay is permanently deformed, which means it has stayed changed.
explain: The word also works for living things. When an illness or injury makes a body part grow or get pushed into an unusual shape, that part is deformed. «Her arm was deformed by the accident.» Here the arm did not just move, its shape was changed.
fact: To deform means to change the normal shape of something.
fact: Things that bounce back, like a rubber band, are elastic; things that stay changed, like modelling clay, are plastic.
fact: Phrases to remember: «deform under pressure», «permanently deformed», «deformed by heat».
fact: In geography, rock layers can deform into folds when continents push together, and this helps form mountains.
fact: The word deform can also describe a body part that grows into an unusual shape because of illness or injury.
exercise: «The heat deformed the plastic ruler.» What does deformed mean here? | *Changed its normal shape | Made it colder | Cut it into small pieces | Made it shine like glass
exercise: In a science test, which material stays deformed after you squash it? | A stretchy elastic band | A spring that bounces back | A rubber ball | *A lump of modelling clay
exercise: In geography, what can make rock layers deform into folds? | *Continents pushing together | Rain falling on the sand | A shadow moving over the town | Ice melting in a glass
test: «Her arm was permanently deformed after the accident.» What does permanently deformed mean? | *Changed in shape for good | Painted bright red | Healed in one day | Covered in mud
test: Which phrase describes a body part that has grown into an unusual shape because of illness? | Full of water | Glowing in the dark | *Deformed by illness | Smiling and happy
exam: A bridge can deform under pressure when heavy trucks cross it. What does this mean? | *Its shape changes when a heavy force pushes on it | It turns into water | It becomes lighter and floats | It stops moving completely
